// The iOS counterpart of `android/local.properties` — the build-time values
// that must not be committed. Copy this file to `Secrets.xcconfig` (gitignored)
// and fill it in. `Debug.xcconfig` and `Release.xcconfig` pull it in with
// `#include?`, so a missing file leaves the values empty and the build still
// runs — the same forgiving behaviour as Gradle's `?: ""` on the Android side.
//
// Note the escaping rule: xcconfig treats `//` as a comment *anywhere* on a
// line, including inside a value. Nothing here contains a URL, which is why
// these are plain; if you ever add one, write it as `http:$()//…`.

// The Maps SDK key, read by AppDelegate.swift via the `GMSApiKey` Info.plist
// entry. **This is not the Android key.** Google restricts an Android key by
// (package name, signing certificate) and an iOS key by bundle identifier, so
// the two platforms need two separate keys from the same Cloud project
// (`789936942272`). An Android key pasted here authenticates nothing and the
// map renders Google's "authorization failure" tile.
//
// Restrict it to `com.siteonlab.zopiqnow` in the Cloud console, and enable
// "Maps SDK for iOS" on the project — it is a different API from the Android
// one and is off by default.
MAPS_API_KEY =

// The **iOS** OAuth client id for Google sign-in, and — like the Maps key —
// not one of the existing ones. `Env.googleWebClientId` stays exactly as it is:
// that is the `serverClientId`, the audience Supabase verifies against, and it
// is platform-independent. This is the separate client that identifies the app
// to Google, the direct analogue of the Android client that is never named in
// Dart either.
//
// Create it as an "iOS" client with bundle id `com.siteonlab.zopiqnow`. It has
// no client secret; iOS clients are public by design.
GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID =

// The same client id with its dot-separated components reversed — Google prints
// it as "iOS URL scheme" on the client's own page, so copy it rather than
// deriving it. It becomes a CFBundleURLScheme, which is how Safari hands the
// sign-in result back to the app.
//
// Looks like: com.googleusercontent.apps.789936942272-abc123def456
GOOGLE_IOS_URL_SCHEME =
